<title>SINGAPORE: Malaysia awards Kekwa crude tender at Tapis -$1.00.</title>
<headline>Malaysia awards Kekwa crude tender at Tapis -$1.00.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Malaysia's oil trading company Petco has awarded its tender to sell Bunga Kekwa crude to a major at Tapis APPI -$1.00 per barrel, free-on-board (fob), industry sources said on Friday.</p>
<p>The tender, which was for a 200-250,000 barrel cargo loading 21-31 August, closed on Thursday.</p>
<p>The tender covers the first shipment of the heavy sweet crude.  </p>
<p>The consortium developing the Bunga Kekwa crude field is made up of Petronas Carigali, with 46.06 percent, Petrovietnam Exploration and Production with 12.5 percent, Canada's International Petroleum Corp with 26.44 percent and Sands Petroleum AB with 15 percent.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65 870 3082)</p>
